   "evidence": "Line 198 `theorem isNormalisedSplit_iff :` and line 205 `theorem NuclearEffect.isNormalisedSplit_iff {E : NuclearEffect} :`, both after `namespace Medium` (line 80) with `namespace NuclearEffect` closed at line 184; the two statements differ (def restatement vs. bridge to `FactorisationHypothesis \u2227 IsNormalised`).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Nuclear/Medium/NuclearEffect.lean",
   "fix": "Rename line 205 to a non-colliding name describing what it says, e.g. `NuclearEffect.isNormalisedSplit_iff_factorisationHypothesis_and_isNormalised`, and make the binder explicit (`(E : NuclearEffect)`) so dot notation works.",
   "issue": "`NuclearEffect.isNormalisedSplit_iff` (line 205) and `isNormalisedSplit_iff` (line 198) are two different statements sharing a short name inside `EpsilonEridani.Nuclear.Medium`: under `open NuclearEffect` the short name is ambiguous, and inside a later `namespace NuclearEffect` it silently resolves to the bridge lemma instead of the definitional restatement. The bridge lemma also keeps `{E : NuclearEffect}` implicit, so `E.isNormalisedSplit_iff` does not elaborate (dot notation fills only the first explicit argument of the namespace's type) and it must always be written out in full \u2014 exactly where the clash bites.",
   "line": 205
